        "comments": "Caenorhabditis sp. 11 is a currently undescribed species. The sequenced strain, JU1373, is an isofemale line isolated by Marie-Anne Felix from a sample collected by Valerie Robert and Loic Sable in January 2008 from rotting torch ginger flowers (Etlingeria elatior) on the island of La Reunion. The species is hermaphroditic with 2.5% males in a laboratory population. The genomic DNA was isolated by Karin Kiontke from mixed populations of males and females of all stages. The expected genome size is estimated to be 90Mb.\n\nThis submission represents sequenced and assembled 454 data from fragment libraries at 9.5X final coverage, from 3kb insert paired end libraries at final 6.4X coverage, and from 20kb paired end libraries at final 4.3X coverage (done at The Genome Center at Washington University).",
